#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:1
msgid "Your first format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:3
msgid ""
"We are going to add support for one report, end to end, and we are going "
"to do it at the level where you write no code at all. The report is a "
"real one — the annual report of a Luxembourg SICAV, whose format is "
"called `ASTERIA-EN24` — and every console block on this page is real "
"output, not an illustration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{doc}`../writing-a-format` is the same path as a checklist, once you have"
" done it once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:10
msgid "What we are aiming at"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:12
msgid "A format is a recipe for one report layout. When it works, this happens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:19
msgid "and the engine can read every report published in that layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:21
msgid "Step 0 — the two things you need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:23
msgid "A formats repository and a report to work on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:31
msgid ""
"`setup-input-db` writes a small list of well-known companies under "
"`tests/input_db/`, called `TEST`. It matters more than it looks: the "
"engine only emits a holding whose investee is **in the list you are "
"searching**. A page full of holdings, none of them in your list, produces"
" nothing at all — and that is correct behaviour, not a failure. Remember "
"this; it will confuse you at least once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:36
msgid "Then put the report where the tests will look for it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:42
msgid "Step 1 — declare that the format exists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:44
msgid ""
"One row in `metadata/formats.csv`, written by components rather than by "
"name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:51
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The name everything else refers to — `ASTERIA-EN24` — is assembled from "
"those components, so a name and its parts cannot drift apart. The year is"
" not decoration: next year's report from the same issuer is a *different "
"format*, because a layout is a snapshot ({doc}`../repository`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:55
msgid "Step 2 — ask the engine what it currently sees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:65
msgid ""
"Everything is unclassified, and that is exactly right: we have not told "
"it anything yet. This is the starting line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:68
msgid ""
"Now open the PDF and find a page of the table you actually want — the "
"list of holdings. Ask yourself one question: **what would let a machine "
"recognise this page and not the others?** Usually it is a heading. In "
"this report every holdings page carries the line *\"Transferable "
"securities admitted to an official stock exchange listing\"*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:73
msgid "Step 3 — find out how that heading is actually set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:75
msgid ""
"You could guess the font. Don't — there is a mode for this. Give "
"`inspect-page` a string and it tells you how the line is really typeset:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:84
msgid ""
"Read that as: font `centurygothic-bold`, size ≈ 7.98, occupying x "
"45.5→307.0 and y 157.6→167.4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:86
msgid ""
"This one command is the answer to most *\"what do I write here?\"* "
"questions. Whenever you are about to invent a font name or a coordinate, "
"search for the text instead and let the report tell you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:89
msgid "Step 4 — classify the pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:91
msgid ""
"Now write the rule, in "
"`content/algorithms/structured/page_classify/args.csv`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:98
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"That is a **selection** — a predicate over the lines of a page, here a "
"font plus a piece of text. The text is matched literally, with `^` and "
"`$` available as anchors and nothing else; it is not a regular expression"
" ({doc}`../selections`). Note that we did not repeat the size: font plus "
"that much text is already unambiguous, and the fewer conditions you pin, "
"the less likely a later page breaks them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:104
msgid "Ask again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:115
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Do not go past this step until it is right.** Classification decides "
"which pages the engine even looks at. If a page you care about is not "
"listed here, no amount of work on the extraction will make it appear — "
"and hunting for the reason in the wrong place is the single most common "
"way to lose an afternoon "
"({doc}`../../../reference/design/classification`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:121
msgid "Step 5 — put the class on the schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:123
msgid ""
"A page class that no step mentions is an error, not a silent no-op. Add "
"it to `content/orchestration/algorithms_schedule.csv`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:131
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"One line, and for a single-class format that is all scheduling ever asks "
"of you ({doc}`../../../reference/design/schedule`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:134
msgid "Step 6 — read the table the way the engine reads it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:136
msgid ""
"Here is the part that makes the structured level feel easy. Ask for the "
"page as a **table**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:154
msgid ""
"The engine has already worked out the grid. The numbers along the top are"
" the column positions, and naming the columns is now just reading them "
"off:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "Column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "Holds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "Configuration field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "the security's name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "*(the anchor — not configured)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "how many"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "Quantity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "the currency it was bought in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "Acquisition currency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "what it cost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "Acquisition cost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "what it is worth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "Market value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "share of net assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:114
msgid "% net assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:166
msgid ""
"So the extraction row, in "
"`content/algorithms/structured/investments/args.csv`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:173
msgid ""
"The three selections before the numbers say where to find, in order, the "
"sub-fund name, the sentence that states the report's currency, and the "
"body of the table. `(:87)` and `(:810)` are vertical bands — *above y=87*"
" for the sub-fund heading, *above y=810* for the body, which is how the "
"page footer is kept out. You find these the same way as everything else: "
"search for a string, read the coordinates it comes back with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:179
msgid "Step 7 — walk the three stages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:181
msgid ""
"A page is processed in three stages, and you can print the output of "
"each. Always in this order, because the first one that looks wrong is the"
" one to fix:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:190
msgid ""
"The middle stage keeps only holdings whose investee is in your list, and "
"attaches everything it understood:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:199
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Everything is still text at this stage — `\"816,173\"`, not a number. "
"That is deliberate: reading the layout and interpreting the meaning are "
"different jobs, and keeping them apart is what lets you tell a layout "
"mistake from a units mistake ({doc}`../../../reference/design/segments`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:203
msgid "The last stage does the interpreting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:211
msgid ""
"Numbers are numbers, the percentage is a fraction, and the fund name has "
"been normalised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:214
msgid ""
"If `txt_blks` comes back **empty** on a page that clearly has holdings, "
"the usual reason is not a bug: none of the companies on that page is in "
"the list you are searching. Try a page you know contains one, or point at"
" a bigger input database with `-I`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:219
msgid "Step 8 — freeze what you have checked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:225
msgid ""
"This writes three JSON fixtures for that page, one per stage. It shows "
"you what it is about to write and asks first — and you should genuinely "
"read it, because `make-tests` records *what the code does now*. Confirm a"
" wrong number here and you have promoted a bug to a specification that "
"the test suite will defend from then on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:230
msgid ""
"Freeze a handful of pages, chosen for being awkward rather than for being"
" many: the first page of a table, a page where it continues, a page with "
"a row that wraps onto two lines. Those are where formats break."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:234
msgid "Step 9 — run the whole report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:241
msgid ""
"Two kinds of test just ran. The per-page ones replay a single page "
"through a single stage — fast, and they name the stage that changed. The "
"whole-document one replays the entire report and compares every output "
"table against `tests/formats/ASTERIA-EN24/out/`. That second one is what "
"actually says the format works: the per-page fixtures can all be green "
"while the scheduling or the deduplication across pages is wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:247
msgid ""
"The first time, there is nothing to compare against, so generate it — "
"deliberately, after reading it. From that moment it is the format's "
"specification, not a snapshot of a run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:250
msgid "Step 10 — say who vouches for it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:252
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The reference output of a format is a claim about the world: *this "
"company appears in this fund for this amount.* The project records who is"
" making the claim and on what basis, and that is what `freeports-"
"validate` is for ({doc}`../../../overview/trust`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:256
msgid "When one row is not enough"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:258
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Sooner or later a report will resist. The escape hatch is graded, not "
"all-or-nothing: the three levels **add up**, so you can keep the "
"structured extraction and write only the filtering in Python, or keep "
"everything and override one deserializer. A hard format should cost more "
"than a simple one — but only in the one place that is hard "
"({doc}`../writing-a-format`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:263
msgid "Two things worth knowing before you meet them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:265
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Company matching is first-match-wins, in the input database's file "
"order.** A holding attributed to the wrong company is often a database "
"problem, not an extraction one ({doc}`../../input-db/index`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/first-format.md:268
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A page that cannot answer everything by itself is not a broken page.** "
"If the fund name is on the cover and the table is on page 412, the table "
"*promises* the name and the cover supplies it later. Reach for that "
"before you reach for making pages depend on each other "
"({doc}`../../../reference/design/promises`)."
msgstr ""

